+This report closes out a second, adversarial audit whose explicit brief was: *try to prove the
+current system is not optimal.* It found four more real bugs (§6), tested seven retrieval/model
+alternatives and rejected all seven with paired confidence intervals (§5.1–5.2), settled the
+CPU-vs-GPU question with a real end-to-end measurement (§5.7), and reconciled this build against two
+independently-produced parallel builds of the same project, adopting the pieces of them that were
+genuinely better and verified (§6.4). The sealed `test2` split — 60 SQuAD-derived scenarios, 3,282
+retrieval qrels, and 754 real spoken HeySQuAD questions per variant — was run exactly once, after
+every architecture and threshold decision was frozen, and is reported in full in §5.8 whether or not
