+
+Every number here is **at least as good as the corresponding development-split number** (§5.8) — the
+system did not overfit to the splits it was tuned on. Official gates G2–G6 pass with `--reps 3` on
+both suites [VERIFIED, §5.9]; the full test suite (185 tests) passes [VERIFIED, §8].
+
+**What changed this audit, with evidence:**
+
+* **A real streaming-accuracy bug was found and fixed, closing the trade-off the last report's
+  headline finding rested on.** The previous report's most-quoted result — "streaming costs ~4 points
+  of answer recall versus the same pipeline run after the user stops talking" — turned out to be an
+  artifact of an orphaned-fragment bug in supersession (§6.1, bug 2). After the fix, streaming and
+  deferred produce **bit-identical** answers on every scored item of the diagnostic set (paired diff
+  0.0% on every metric) while streaming still removes essentially all of the post-speech delay (p95
+  47 ms vs. 1,672 ms) [VERIFIED, §5.5]. The latency/accuracy trade-off this project was built to solve
+  is, on this evidence, no longer a trade-off.
+* **A second decomposition bug and a synthesis duplication bug were found and fixed.** Exact
+  decomposition — the sub-query count matching the gold count exactly — rose from 90%/65%
+  (dev/diagnostic) to **100%/100%** after both fixes (§6.1, bugs 1 and 2); over-split rate fell to 0%.
+* **Seven retrieval/model alternatives were tested and rejected, all with paired significance**:
+  larger reranker (MiniLM-L12, −1.5pt r@1), swapped embedder (BGE-small, −1.3pt), smaller reranker
+  (TinyBERT, −6.2pt), a SQuAD2 extractive reader used as the *primary* answer selector instead of a
+  refusal signal (−1.8 to −9.1pt vs. the cross-encoder selector on 3 of 4 spoken-question sets), a
+  character n-gram retrieval channel for ASR robustness (no significant gain), a corpus-vocabulary
+  typo corrector (+1.1pt r@1, CI crosses zero), and GPU inference (§5.1–5.4, §5.7).
+* **GPU was benchmarked end-to-end and rejected as the default, with a number, not an assumption.**
+  Isolated micro-benchmarks show the reader model is 5–8× faster on the machine's MX250 GPU via
+  ONNX Runtime's CUDA provider. Run through the *whole* pipeline in real time, GPU vs. CPU make **no
+  measurable difference** (678.2 s vs. 685.0 s wall time for an identical 60-scenario replay,
+  byte-identical answers) because speculative prefetch already finishes the expensive calls while the
+  user is still talking — the thing GPU would speed up is not on the critical path. CPU stays the
+  verified default; GPU is now a documented, opt-in `STREAMING_RAG_ORT_PROVIDER=cuda` switch that
+  changes nothing about the default configuration (§5.7).
+* **The refusal gate was re-fit on corrected data and re-frozen at essentially the same operating
+  point.** An override-parsing bug in the eval harness (§6.1, bug 5) had silently corrupted one
+  threshold sweep; after the fix, refitting the gate from scratch on the same deployment assumption
+  (30% of questions unanswerable, a wrong answer costs as much as a correct one is worth) reproduces
+  the deployed threshold (0.40) and nearly identical coefficients — the deployed gate was not stale.
+* **This build was reconciled against two other builds of the same project** that existed on this
+  machine (§6.4). The reconciliation surfaced two more real bugs — the synthesizer blocked the event
+  loop for up to 80 ms per turn on a prefetch miss, and a `zip()` combining the refusal model's
+  parameters would have silently dropped features on a length mismatch — both fixed and now covered
+  by regression tests ported from that build. An entire opt-in subsystem (LLM-backed generative
+  synthesis, with per-claim verification) was also merged in; it changes nothing about the default
+  extractive path and is explicitly **not measured against gold answers** (§7, §10).
+
+**What still doesn't work, reported with the same prominence:**
+
+* **Decomposition is still weak on real, unpunctuated ASR speech specifically.** HeySQuAD-ASR answer
+  recall (56.0% sealed, 37–56% on the tuning splits) trails HeySQuAD-clean (85.9% sealed) by 22–33
+  points across every split. The mechanism is now well isolated (§5.5, §10.1): decomposition depends
+  on punctuation, and real ASR transcripts have none.
+* **A SQuAD2-trained reader is used inside the refusal gate for data whose corpus overlaps SQuAD's
+  source domain.** The reader never saw these exact articles, but the *question style* is in-domain,
+  which likely flatters the gate's measured precision (§9, §10.4).
+* **The generative-synthesis path (§7) is wired, tested for structural correctness, and completely
+  unmeasured on gold answers.** No LLM provider key was available in this environment.
 
