+### 6.3 Resource search — no further adoption
+
+Explicit web research this audit for untried open-source levers (§ "research findings" below) found:
+a larger extractive reader (roberta-base-squad2, +3.5 F1 on SQuAD2 for ~4× the parameters) unlikely to
+reverse the already-significant reader-vs-CE loss (§5.3); no lightweight library for compound-question
+decomposition better than a rule-based approach under this project's offline/CPU constraint; SymSpell,
+algorithmically identical to the already-tested vocabulary corrector (§5.4); FlashRank/mxbai-rerank-v2
+for tighter CPU latency, not adopted because latency is not the current bottleneck (§5.7). Nothing
+found cleared the bar for adoption; each is logged as a specific, evidenced rejection rather than
+asserted away.
+
+### 6.4 Reconciliation with parallel builds
+
+Independently of this session, two other builds of this same Theme 4 project existed on this machine
+and were merged, by a separate process, into a `streaming-live-rag-merged` workspace whose own
+`MERGE_NOTES.md` documents the merge in detail. That merge correctly identified this build's
+retrieval, controller and default synthesis as the strongest of the three (sealed r@1 90.1% vs. 71.8%
+for the weakest; exact decomposition 90%→100% here vs. 35% for the weakest), reproduced this build's
+sealed numbers item-for-item, and surfaced two genuine bugs (§6.1, bugs 6–7) plus a missing
+`tests/__init__.py` (bug 8) this audit had not caught. Those fixes, their regression tests
+(`tests/session/test_adversarial.py`), and one wholly-additive subsystem — LLM-backed generative
+synthesis (§7) — were pulled into this build and verified: the full suite now passes at **185/185**
+(103 before this audit + 67 ported from the generative subsystem/adversarial tests + 15 new this
+audit), and a full dev-set re-run after the merge reproduced **byte-identical** answers to before it,
+confirming the merge changed nothing about the verified default path.
+
+One change from that other exploration was **not** adopted: a config edit that set
+`synthesis.refusal_gate` to `"none"` by default, based on the same raw-answer-recall-only finding
+discussed and rejected in §5.6. It was found, reverted, and is documented in §5.6 as a
+considered-and-rejected alternative rather than silently discarded — per this audit's standing rule
+that nothing gets tuned to make numbers look better without the accompanying cost being shown.
 
